The <derivative> of a distribution is defined by integration by parts. Therefore
$$
\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}f(t)\delta'(t)dt
=-\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}f'(t)\delta(t)dt
=-f'(0).
$$

